    "full_text": "# 14. OpenRISC 1200 SoC Architecture & IP Specifications\n\nThe final section of *Practical UVM: Step by Step* showcases an entire, tape-out capable **OpenRISC 1200 System-on-Chip (SoC)** combining all verified IP blocks:\n\n### OpenRISC SoC Hardware Specifications:\n- **Processor Core (`or1200`)**: 32-bit scalar RISC Harvard architecture with DSP MAC support.\n- **Interconnect (`wb_conmax`)**: Wishbone multi-master crossbar connecting CPU, DMA, Ethernet, USB, and memory controllers.\n- **Memory Controllers**: Synchronous DRAM (`wb_sdram_ctrl`), On-Chip ROM, and CFI Flash controller.\n- **Peripherals & Interfaces**:\n  - 10/100 Mbps Ethernet MAC (`ethmac`)\n  - USB 1.1 Host/Slave controller (`usbhostslave`)\n  - UART 16550 serial transceiver (`uart16550`)\n  - SPI master controller (`simple_spi` / `spi_ctrl`)\n  - I2C master/slave controller (`i2c_master_slave`)\n  - General Purpose I/O (`gpio`)\n  - JTAG TAP controller (`jtag_tap`)\n  - VGA / Color LCD Controller (`vga_lcd`)\n\nThis module covers top-level SoC simulation, memory map configuration, and multi-core chip bring-up.\n",
